<title>VENEZUELA: CANTV rate increase delayed.</title>
<headline>CANTV rate increase delayed.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scheduled third quarter rate increases for Venezuelan telephone company CANTV are still awaiting approval by telecom watchdog Conatel and have been delayed, Transport and Communications Minister Moises Orozco told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Clearly the increase will not happen by July 1,&quot; Orozco said. After Conatel's approval, the increase must be discussed by the economic cabinet, Orozco added.</p>
<p>CANTV has said it expects an average rate increase of 1.98 percent, following the second quarter rise of 4.18 percent granted April 14.</p>
<p>((-- Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
